# Seed completeness (home + editorial)

When adding any **new** event seed id (`fallback.*.json` or `recurring.*.json`), finish **all** of the following before calling the work done. Incomplete seeds are not shippable.

## 1. Home Recently added (required)

1. Add the same event `id` to `SEED_CREATED_AT` in `src/lib/seed-created-at.ts`
2. Default: commit-day noon UTC, e.g. `"2026-09-09T12:00:00.000Z"`
3. **Same-day batch order:** if several new ids share a commit day and you care which cards lead Recently added, stagger times (newest first) — e.g. `16:00`, `15:00`, `14:00`, `13:00` UTC — instead of identical noon. Ties break on event `id` (locale-stable), **not** title; localized titles must never be relied on for rail order
4. Without `SEED_CREATED_AT`, the event page can work while home **Recently added** omits it (`getNewHighlightEvents` requires `createdAt` within 14 days)
5. **Card titles for series / multi-day programs:** lead with what differs (venue or role), put the shared brand second — e.g. `Hard Rock Host Day — Descubre Sosúa`, not `Descubre Sosúa 2026 — Host Meetup…` — so truncated home cards stay distinguishable across EN/ES/FR
6. **Titles must be catalog-unique (required):** `mergeUniqueEvents` in `src/lib/public-events.ts` dedupes by a normalized **title** key, not only by `id`. A new dated night that reuses the same EN/ES/FR title as an older seed (even a past one still in `fallback.*.json`) is **silently dropped** — event page may 404 from rails and **Recently added never shows it**. Before shipping:
   - Grep existing seeds for the same/near-same title (all three locales)
   - For repeat nights (Bandoleras, House Friday, karaoke series, etc.), make the title distinct — prefer **venue + series** or include the calendar day, e.g. `Ambar Lounge Bandoleras — Carlos Rivera`, not another bare `Bandoleras Fridays — Carlos Rivera`
   - Distinct `id` alone is **not** enough

## 2. Event POP opinion (required)

1. Add a unique seed opinion for the new event `id` in `src/lib/event-opinions-seed.ts` or `src/lib/event-opinions-seed-more.ts`
2. Copy must be specific (contrast + tradeoff or practical send), EN body plus ES/FR `localized`, with `priceFeel` / `priceNote` when useful
3. Do **not** ship a generic recycled blurb. Prefer Google Places / official research; if evidence is thin, write a cautious specific tip from verified schedule/venue facts — do not leave the event without an opinion
4. Server ingest drafts (`eventOpinionDrafts`) are a backup for live crawls, **not** a substitute for seeding opinions on new seed events in-repo

## 3. New venue tip + assessment (required when the venue is new)

When introducing a **new** `venueSlug` (or first time that slug gets a seeded listing):

1. Unique tip in `VENUE_TIP_COPY` (`src/lib/venue-assessment-tips.ts`) — EN `body` + ES/FR `localized`
2. Matching `editorial({ venueSlug: ... })` entry in `SEED_VENUE_ASSESSMENTS` (`src/lib/venue-assessments-seed.ts`) — `editorial()` throws if the tip body is missing
3. Wire venue seed / i18n / image / attributions as usual

When only adding events at an **existing** venue, refresh the tip if the new nights meaningfully change the guest send; otherwise leave the existing tip.

## 4. Images (required with new seeds)

1. **If the user attaches flyer / event images with the request, use those.** Copy into `public/events/` (and `popevent-images/` when used), wire `EVENT_IMAGE_FILES` in `src/lib/event-images.ts`, update `scripts/sync-event-images.mjs` if needed, and note them in `public/events/ATTRIBUTIONS.md` as POP-supplied / editor-provided. Do **not** skip attached assets in favor of venue fallback, Maps scraping, or Instagram CDN pulls.
2. When no image is attached, source authentic heroes from Google Maps/Places, official sites, ticket OG, press, Wikimedia, or a POP photo of *this* place — **not** by scraping Instagram/Facebook (see `public/events/ATTRIBUTIONS.md`). Venue lounge fallback is OK only when no event-specific asset exists.
3. **Never put texted promo art behind Discover / city photo heroes.** Flyers with baked-in type (titles, prices, “SÁBADOS”, logos as design chrome) go in `HOME_HERO_TYPOGRAPHY_HEAVY_FILES` and must **not** be added to `HOME_HERO_SCENE_FILES`. Home/city heroes only use opt-in scene/place shots (or city/coast fallbacks). Event cards and detail pages may still use the flyer.
4. **Compress editor-supplied images before commit** — JPEG max width **1200px**, mozjpeg quality ~**82–85** (same defaults as `scripts/optimize-venue-images.mjs` / sync `writeDest`). Do not check in multi‑MB phone dumps. Prefer compressing locally over waiting for CI optimize.
5. **Filename bump on replace** — when swapping a curated event or venue hero, change the filename (`-v2`, descriptive suffix) and update `event-images.ts` / `venue-images.ts` (+ sync maps + attributions). PWA/detail heroes strip query cache-busts, so a new path is required.
6. Also wire attributions, curated `isFree` / tickets / phone maps, and EN/ES/FR seed parity.
